        "problem": "Evaluate ${}_{10}{C}_{1}.$",
        "worked_solution": "In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=10$ and $r=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{10}{C}_{1} & =\\frac{10!}{(10-1)!\\,1!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10!}{9!\\,1!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\cdot \\cancel{9!}}{\\cancel{9!}1!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{1} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
